rhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":80.4,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013394626985913765,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":77.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.06866,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":45.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Bank OZK operates as a full-service Arkansas state-chartered bank that provides retail and commercial banking services. The company provides deposit services, including non-interest-bearing checking, interest bearing transaction, business sweep, savings, money market, individual retirement, and other accounts, as well as time and reciprocal deposits. It offers trust and wealth services, such as personal trusts, custodial accounts, investment management accounts, and retirement accounts; corporate trust services that include trustee, paying agent and registered transfer agent services, and other related services; and treasury management services, which include automated clearing house, wire transfer, current and prior day transaction reporting, wholesale lockbox, remote deposit capture, automated credit line transfer, reconciliation, positive pay, commercial card, and other services, as well as zero balance and investment sweep accounts. In addition, the company provides real estate, consumer, small business, indirect recreational vehicle and marine, equipment, agricultural, commercial and industrial, government guaranteed, lines of credit, homebuilder, and housing loans; lender and structured, business aviation, and subscription financing services; and mortgage and other lending products. The company was formerly known as Bank of the Ozarks and changed its name to Bank OZK in July 2018. Bank OZK was founded in 1903 and is headquartered in Little Rock, Arkansas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. George G. Gleason II | Chairman & CEO | Age 71 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $531K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $225K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Bank OZK is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.5B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","The business throws off $732M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 42 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 6.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average SGA growth (15% YoY) warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 53% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Fulcrum Asset Management LLP Purchases 13,868 Shares of Bank OZK $OZK","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/fulcrum-asset-management-llp-purchases-13868-shares-of-bank-ozk-ozk.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794559753.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (OZK) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/38/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_OZK_Movement_111226102002_1794540002.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794540002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bank OZK $OZK Stake Lowered by Cabot Wealth Management Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/bank-ozk-ozk-stake-lowered-by-cabot-wealth-management-inc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794475543.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.929,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bank OZK FY2026 Earnings Forecast Boosted by Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/bank-ozk-fy2026-earnings-forecast-boosted-by-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794399274.0,"origin":